  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f: \\mathbf{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbf{R}$ be a function given by\n$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\frac{1-\\cos 2 x}{x^2}, & x < 0 \\\\\n\\alpha, & x=0, \\\\\n\\frac{\\beta \\sqrt{1-\\cos x}}{x}, & x>0\n\\end{array}\\right.$\nwhere $\\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbf{R}$. If $f$ is continuous at $x=0$, then $\\alpha^2+\\beta^2$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
