  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & f\\left(0^{-}\\right)=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{-}} \\frac{2 \\sin ^2 x}{x^2}=2=\\alpha \\\\ & f\\left(0^{+}\\right)=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} \\beta \\times \\sqrt{2} \\frac{\\sin \\frac{x}{2}}{2 \\frac{x}{2}}=\\frac{\\beta}{\\sqrt{2}}=2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\beta=2 \\sqrt{2} \\\\ & \\alpha^2+\\beta^2=4+8=12\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
